[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62224,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mature teratoma is a tumour composed exclusively of mature tissues derived from two or three germ layers (ectoderm, mesoderm, and/or endoderm).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62225,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9080/0 Teratoma, benign</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62226,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F32.Y &amp; XH3GV5 Other specified benign neoplasm of ovary &amp; Teratoma, benign</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62227,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> mature cystic teratoma</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> dermoid cyst; mature solid teratoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62228,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62229,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62230,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases occur in women of reproductive age. Abdominal pain or mass is common; some cases are detected incidentally. Rarely, young women may present with anti-NMDAR encephalitis {22833082; 25272299; 31021857}. About 10% of cases are bilateral {13238472; 16990705} [[Scully RE, Young RH, Clement PB. Tumors of the ovary, maldeveloped gonads, fallopian tube and broad ligament. Washington, DC: Armed Forces Institute of Pathology; 1998. (AFIP atlas of tumor pathology, series 3; fascicle 23).]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62231,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours account for 20% of all ovarian neoplasms in pathological studies {13238472; 16990705} [[Scully RE, Young RH, Clement PB. Tumors of the ovary, maldeveloped gonads, fallopian tube and broad ligament. Washington, DC: Armed Forces Institute of Pathology; 1998. (AFIP atlas of tumor pathology, series 3; fascicle 23).]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62232,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62233,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The favoured explanation is the parthenogenetic theory, which suggests an origin from the primordial germ cell {162806; 5476662; 5921072; 6363699; 28664933}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62234,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most are cystic (mature cystic teratoma) but some can be solid. They are usually 5&ndash;10&nbsp;cm but are much smaller (average: 1.9&nbsp;cm) in women with anti-NMDAR encephalitis {13238472; 31021857}. The cysts contain sebaceous material, hair, and sometimes teeth or cartilage. A solid nodule lined by hair-bearing skin (Rokitansky protuberance) is typically present along the cyst lining. Mature solid teratoma is solid with interspersed cysts {4722922; 13362421}. Those resembling a malformed human fetus have been termed fetiform teratoma {6724790}. Solid areas should be liberally sampled (ideally, one section per centimetre of solid area).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62235,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ectodermal derivatives include squamous epithelium and cutaneous adnexal structures, as well as neuroectoderm (glia, ependyma, and cerebellum). Mesodermal derivatives include adipose, bone, cartilage, and smooth muscle. Endodermal derivatives include gastrointestinal and respiratory/bronchial epithelium, thyroid, and salivary glands. Rarely, prostate {12068172}, pituitary, adrenal, and parathyroid tissue can be seen. Rare microscopic foci of immature neural tissue may be present {3429105}. Fat necrosis and foreign body reaction to keratin are common. In patients with anti-NMDAR encephalitis, neuroglial tissues are surrounded by lymphoid aggregates with germinal centres {31021857; 22833082}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62236,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 90,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:49:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
